Kind: ablation
Issue: #807
Takes out: pmap_enter()'s refusal of a leaf larger than 4 KiB -- pmap_verbs_selftest()'s unmapping branch then takes the direct map's leaf at the base away, and pmap_forget() drops the kernel pmap's resident count for a leaf it never counted, which is zero at that point of the boot: the machine stops there and names the address, before the self-test can say anything; on a kernel whose count were not zero the self-test's own WRONG would be the line
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 4
Expect: pmap: resident_count underflow at va 0xffff800000000000|UrMach x86-64: pmap_enter NONE over the [0-9]+ KiB leaf at the direct map's base -> not refused, WRONG
Note: Judged under QEMU (TCG and KVM), pmap_verbs_selftest(), on victus 02/11/2026 at 54555cb5: the ablated tree caught 4 of 4 and the fixed tree passed 4 of 4, every ablated boot stopping at the resident count's underflow at 0xffff800000000000 right after the self-test's pmap_remove line.  A first run at 22198036 expected only the self-test's WRONG, which never comes, and caught 0 of 4 boots that had all stopped there.  Judged again on the union of the critical fixes, 72778d46, on victus 02/11/2026: caught 4 of 4, and the fixed tree passed 4 of 4.

